<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:49:29Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>India's citizen-led school audits test limits of activism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bdd8f191e47608801375af4f52dce310c05fe5cc065ffcb9508a72c8b4ebe6a2</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-citizen-led-school-audits-test-limits-of-activism/a-78545789--a961d5089d76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-citizen-led-school-audits-test-limits-of-activism/a-78545789?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The student-led "Cockroach" movement is taking its campaign for accountability to government schools, but the activists' methods are encountering growing resistance from authorities.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal issues fresh flood warning as 3,000 still missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ea7f1d17ae8e9a08d2b213cc79edb51b65ebca7b6245076dff778e096d0e9aa</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T06:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-issues-fresh-flood-warning-as-3-000-still-missing/a-78561068--6dc0447b7ea8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-issues-fresh-flood-warning-as-3-000-still-missing/a-78561068?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rescuers are trying to reach dozens of hydropower workers trapped in flooded tunnels, but have been hampered by further rainfall.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: PM Modi in Uzbekistan on way to SCO summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:520b2ef614be8528f9d5f7e29e78d74dc68b20754ea10d89acba6aeaf778503e</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T15:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-pm-modi-in-uzbekistan-on-way-to-sco-summit/live-78554796--37c039cf0336.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-pm-modi-in-uzbekistan-on-way-to-sco-summit/live-78554796?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi is in Uzbekistan for a two-day state visit, after which he will go to Kyrgyzstan for the SCO Summit. Meanwhile, hundreds of Indians are still missing in Nepal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Death toll from Nepal-Tibet floods rises to over 600</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ebafef274c67afdfa0f8caafc2bfc0b1d5f0aee026023203c7ec3ea892dbdb5</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/death-toll-from-nepal-tibet-floods-rises-to-over-600/a-78555290--1fcc613e6307.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/death-toll-from-nepal-tibet-floods-rises-to-over-600/a-78555290?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Heavy rain is complicating an already difficult rescue effort, as hundreds remain missing three days after deadly flash floods hit the Nepal-Tibet border region.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea leans toward military conscription for women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:812167d24af450dd8684a7631a69f8fe2f3d28d086ce24ab62a1e92af8078e04</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-leans-toward-military-conscription-for-women/a-78547426--a0344d8b90da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-leans-toward-military-conscription-for-women/a-78547426?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing a population decline, fewer potential service members and calls for social equality to be extended to national military service, Korea is inching closer to breaking the taboo on women on the front line.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tragedy in Nepal: How do flash floods happen?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a2b4bd5a83981c539edf0d2af4f52ff8ecf0f75154b9e2ddd2c76bef1b0e047</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T14:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tragedy-in-nepal-how-do-flash-floods-happen/a-78526421--33dcb9d81b48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tragedy-in-nepal-how-do-flash-floods-happen/a-78526421?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When flash floods sweep through the Himalayas, there is often little time to react. Scientists are working to understand the risks and improve early warning systems.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>The great lake divide: Collapse vs. comeback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec26f48151e57e1822692a2fa897f6de56a589e7bba0d154dd20301dab5f9b32</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T09:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-great-lake-divide-collapse-vs-comeback/a-78460263--c6617e04516d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-great-lake-divide-collapse-vs-comeback/a-78460263?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As some of the world's biggest lakes vanish in real time, others are proving that recovery is still within reach.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Gamescom 2026: What's next for the gaming industry?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:681804192f39274e24062c6b344088109935b81cad228f791045f619ff88ea14</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T11:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gamescom-2026-what-s-next-for-the-gaming-industry/a-78502849--ab23dbafb15c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gamescom-2026-what-s-next-for-the-gaming-industry/a-78502849?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Gamescom 2026 opens in Cologne, AI, hardware costs and slowing user growth are putting pressure on the global games industry despite its current strength.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>India: Assam tea industry faces climate-driven labor crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1db8da970139594434af2cb0a5aeadc4095b57b2adc7afc61e8be1f3919973e</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-assam-tea-industry-faces-climate-driven-labor-crisis/a-78506414--da42632fff84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-assam-tea-industry-faces-climate-driven-labor-crisis/a-78506414?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Plantations in Assam produce more than half of India's tea. But rising heat is hurting yields, workers are increasingly leaving for more stable work, and producers are feeling the squeeze of stagnant tea prices.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why land mines are back in force despite international bans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:312b70aae48b51f3222a32f730b7cf9e203c41efa4dabe70e723e8cc0b04de82</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:49:29Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T05:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-land-mines-are-back-in-force-despite-international-bans/a-78501702--b1342c3732f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-land-mines-are-back-in-force-despite-international-bans/a-78501702?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's war on Ukraine has prompted several European countries to abandon a landmark 1990s land mine treaty. DW examines what's at stake.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Will Iran withdraw from nuclear non-proliferation treaty?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da8722237ffc80333c70abf324454b8b923f038b8dfcf2df0d110eb7ee2cbdc9</id><updated>2026-08-31T05:48:37Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T12:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-iran-withdraw-from-nuclear-non-proliferation-treaty/a-78495930--d893e8d6ca46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-iran-withdraw-from-nuclear-non-proliferation-treaty/a-78495930?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian lawmakers have again raised the possibility of leaving a decades-old international nuclear weapons treaty. Analysts say the threat to quit may offer Tehran more leverage than an actual withdrawal.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
